WEBVTT

00:06.506 --> 00:08.508
[no sound from screens]

00:08.591 --> 00:10.593
[faint, muffled rumbling]

00:11.594 --> 00:13.221
[suspenseful music playing]

00:16.099 --> 00:17.559
[echoing children's laughter]

00:18.393 --> 00:19.978
[breathing shakily]

00:21.938 --> 00:23.690
- [bleep]
- [device ringing]

00:24.691 --> 00:26.443
I won't let anyone else die.

00:27.027 --> 00:29.654
If we work together,
I'm sure we can all escape.

00:31.823 --> 00:34.534
- [gasping]
- [Arisu] Let's try to beat this, together.

00:35.368 --> 00:37.120
[Rei] Sounds like a good idea.

00:37.954 --> 00:40.832
[Arisu] Nobu, you'll be heading
away from the exit,

00:40.915 --> 00:44.586
but can you return to C3
and meet up with Rei, who's in C4?

00:45.086 --> 00:49.132
The starting room has no point deduction,
so it's the room with the least risk.

00:56.389 --> 00:57.515
Understood.

00:58.183 --> 01:00.310
Usagi has the most points left.

01:03.063 --> 01:05.273
I have more points because
the child's with me.

01:07.192 --> 01:09.319
Do you think you can head to room A3?

01:10.278 --> 01:13.281
There's a risk that it's a room
with a high points deduction.

01:16.701 --> 01:17.827
I got this.

01:19.704 --> 01:21.081
That means one person

01:21.664 --> 01:23.208
will have to stay behind.

01:23.708 --> 01:25.460
- [grunting]
- [Sachiko whimpering] No!

01:26.961 --> 01:28.838
- [husband] Huh?
- [Sachiko gasping]

01:30.340 --> 01:31.925
- [husband yells]
- [Sachiko sobs]

01:32.675 --> 01:34.803
[boy] Careful. Are you all right?

01:34.886 --> 01:36.346
I'll take over from here.

01:37.514 --> 01:38.890
Thank you, son.

01:38.973 --> 01:40.558
[poignant music playing]

01:40.642 --> 01:41.768
[sighs]

01:53.238 --> 01:54.781
- [bleep]
- [device ringing]

01:54.864 --> 01:56.491
Arisu, I'll stay here.

01:57.575 --> 01:58.576
[Ryuji] Why you?

02:00.078 --> 02:03.289
Because I'm the eldest here.
And it's my choice.

02:04.082 --> 02:07.127
Let us old folks take care
of the dangerous stuff.

02:07.710 --> 02:11.005
And you kids,
your job is to take care of the future.

02:15.468 --> 02:16.511
[PA chimes]

02:16.594 --> 02:20.598
[computer] Players, hold your wristband
up to your chosen door

02:20.682 --> 02:22.976
and proceed to the next room.

02:23.059 --> 02:24.727
Don't worry, I'm okay!

02:36.239 --> 02:38.575
[whirring]

03:02.932 --> 03:04.934
[Yuna sobbing]

03:25.121 --> 03:26.164
[sighs]

03:26.247 --> 03:27.790
[door mechanism hisses]

03:31.878 --> 03:33.880
[theme music playing]

04:35.984 --> 04:36.818
[PA chimes]

04:36.901 --> 04:40.446
[computer] B4 is a minus two points room.

04:41.114 --> 04:44.826
Please select whose points will be used.

04:45.910 --> 04:47.745
Let's use my points this time.

04:48.538 --> 04:50.081
[beep]

04:50.164 --> 04:53.251
Points deduction confirmed.

04:56.421 --> 04:57.630
[Usagi gasps]

04:59.424 --> 05:00.883
[PA chimes]

05:00.967 --> 05:05.305
A3 is a minus eight points room.

05:05.388 --> 05:08.975
Please select whose points will be used.

05:09.058 --> 05:10.935
[melancholy music playing]

05:11.019 --> 05:12.145
[sighs]

05:12.812 --> 05:14.814
I promise to protect you.

05:16.190 --> 05:17.358
[whirs and bleeps]

05:19.068 --> 05:21.946
Points deduction confirmed.

05:22.447 --> 05:23.614
[device ringing]

05:23.698 --> 05:24.699
Usagi.

05:24.782 --> 05:26.034
What about Tetsu?

05:29.495 --> 05:31.164
[sighs shakily]

05:33.750 --> 05:34.751
I get it.

05:35.251 --> 05:37.253
[jumbled, blaring sounds]

05:38.629 --> 05:41.341
[whimpers] Tetsu!

05:47.263 --> 05:48.681
Tetsu…

05:53.436 --> 05:54.979
[sobbing]

05:57.148 --> 06:00.777
A3 is a minus eight points room.

06:01.444 --> 06:03.571
If we were in that room, we'd be dead.

06:04.614 --> 06:08.201
I'm the last one.
None of us can come through here again.

06:09.827 --> 06:11.537
[computer] Eleventh round.

06:11.621 --> 06:12.705
Start.

06:12.789 --> 06:15.708
[sighs] Time to release Sachiko
from lockdown.

06:20.880 --> 06:23.883
To create a horizontal line
between A3 and C3,

06:23.966 --> 06:26.344
Usagi and Nobu need
to stay where they are.

06:26.427 --> 06:28.679
But Nobu only has two points left.

06:29.180 --> 06:32.683
So even if he tries to meet up
with Sachiko once she's released,

06:32.767 --> 06:34.936
we can't make it work with zero points.

06:36.479 --> 06:38.898
Well, in that case,
I could meet up with Nobu at C3

06:38.981 --> 06:40.191
and make a horizontal line?

06:40.274 --> 06:41.275
No.

06:41.359 --> 06:44.153
Even if you go to C3 to connect with Nobu,

06:44.237 --> 06:47.657
you'll never be able to reach A5
even with both your points.

06:48.241 --> 06:49.450
[buzzer sounds]

06:49.534 --> 06:53.663
[Arisu] Rei, I want you to stay where
you are at C4, so you can save Sachiko.

06:54.163 --> 06:55.957
And then meet up with Nobu there.

06:56.457 --> 06:57.625
Understood.

06:58.793 --> 07:03.256
[Usagi] If I head to A2, I can form
a diagonal line with Rei at C4.

07:03.756 --> 07:05.675
I'll take my child to A2.

07:07.135 --> 07:09.804
But, Usagi,
none of us have been in that room.

07:09.887 --> 07:14.183
I know. But my child and I,
we both have seven points left.

07:14.267 --> 07:17.770
There's a possibility that A2 has
an even bigger points deduction.

07:17.854 --> 07:20.064
Even if your plan works, Usagi,
if you're in lockdown,

07:20.148 --> 07:21.107
none of us can help you.

07:21.190 --> 07:25.027
One mistake and we'll never be
able to make it back to A5. [gasps]

07:25.111 --> 07:26.821
[tense music playing]

07:27.989 --> 07:29.449
We don't have time. What do we do?

07:29.532 --> 07:31.492
[gasps] What can we do?

07:33.035 --> 07:35.705
How can everyone make
it out of here alive?

07:36.873 --> 07:38.291
What can we do?

07:41.461 --> 07:43.337
[Usagi] Arisu, there must be a way!

07:45.006 --> 07:46.591
We've done it before.

07:47.300 --> 07:49.802
We've fought and won all the games so far.

07:50.845 --> 07:52.513
[gasping shakily]

07:55.183 --> 07:57.185
All those friends who kept me alive.

08:12.783 --> 08:14.368
Every game includes

08:14.869 --> 08:16.454
a clue on how to survive.

08:21.125 --> 08:22.960
[gasping]

08:29.884 --> 08:31.511
[music quietens]

08:44.023 --> 08:45.900
[tense music resumes]

08:53.115 --> 08:54.450
The wristband.

08:56.369 --> 08:57.912
[gasps]

08:57.995 --> 08:59.080
We use the wristband.

08:59.830 --> 09:00.790
The wristband?

09:00.873 --> 09:04.377
Usagi, in A2, place the child's wristband.

09:05.628 --> 09:09.090
Place only the child's wristband.
Even though the child isn't wearing it,

09:09.173 --> 09:11.259
it's been working so far.

09:11.759 --> 09:13.970
And that means,
if we put the wristband inside,

09:14.053 --> 09:15.680
the plan should still work.

09:15.763 --> 09:17.223
[chiming]

09:21.394 --> 09:22.979
Makes no sense.

09:24.272 --> 09:27.733
He's right. What happens
if the poor child dies trying to save me?

09:29.026 --> 09:30.152
I know.

09:30.236 --> 09:33.030
Even if we clear the game,
if the wristband stays inside

09:33.114 --> 09:34.907
and the points are zero, Usagi could die.

09:34.991 --> 09:36.284
You've no way of knowing!

09:38.077 --> 09:41.289
But what if… we find a way
to retrieve the wristband?

09:41.372 --> 09:42.623
How do you do that?

09:42.707 --> 09:46.460
If Usagi goes back for the wristband,
we'll be back where we started.

09:46.544 --> 09:48.546
[tense music continues]

09:55.219 --> 09:56.929
- [sobbing]
- You can't be in here!

09:57.013 --> 09:59.473
- You have to go with Rei!
- Yuna! Come with me.

09:59.557 --> 10:01.601
- Come on!
- [Arisu] Yuna, please!

10:01.684 --> 10:03.185
[Yuna sobbing]

10:04.520 --> 10:07.315
Earlier, when Rei was
about to enter this room,

10:07.398 --> 10:10.526
her wristband was on the other side
of the door and it didn't react.

10:11.068 --> 10:15.489
So that means, if my wristband
stays inside A3, then I should be okay.

10:16.198 --> 10:19.910
You just reach your arm into the room
and you grab the child's wristband.

10:20.620 --> 10:22.872
Usagi, can you do it?

10:25.333 --> 10:26.250
I can do it.

10:26.334 --> 10:28.502
Yes, but once the wristband
is back inside,

10:28.586 --> 10:30.379
eight points will be deducted again.

10:30.463 --> 10:33.424
Even if you return the wristband
from A2 to A3,

10:33.507 --> 10:36.802
neither of them will have enough
points to reach the exit.

10:42.808 --> 10:44.810
[Yuna crying]

10:48.856 --> 10:50.524
YUNA ITSUKI 11, RYOHEI ARISU 6

11:01.202 --> 11:02.161
Yuna…

11:04.664 --> 11:05.998
I need a favor.

11:08.417 --> 11:10.044
[Yuna continues crying]

11:10.127 --> 11:12.713
Some of us will need your help to survive.

11:15.716 --> 11:17.802
Yuna, we need you to save us.

11:22.848 --> 11:24.642
- Please, help us.
- [whimpers]

11:34.068 --> 11:35.444
[gasps]

11:44.829 --> 11:48.207
Nobu, move across to C4
and we'll meet up together. Got it?

11:48.290 --> 11:49.667
Understood.

11:49.750 --> 11:50.793
[chiming]

11:50.876 --> 11:54.880
[computer] Players, hold your wristband
up to your chosen door

11:54.964 --> 11:57.717
and proceed to the next room.

12:02.722 --> 12:04.306
[whirring]

12:04.390 --> 12:06.100
[music fades]

12:09.437 --> 12:10.604
[sighs]

12:11.105 --> 12:12.314
I'm sorry.

12:12.815 --> 12:15.776
I'll come back for you. I promise.

12:15.860 --> 12:17.862
[muffled voices on screens]

12:17.945 --> 12:19.655
[panting]

12:21.657 --> 12:22.742
[gasps]

12:30.791 --> 12:32.501
[mechanism hisses]

12:32.585 --> 12:33.794
[wristband pings]

12:34.879 --> 12:36.964
[melancholy, suspenseful music playing]

12:39.925 --> 12:41.635
[door mechanism hisses]

12:44.138 --> 12:45.431
[sighs]

12:58.652 --> 13:00.863
[husband] You're worthless! I'll kill you!

13:00.946 --> 13:02.865
- [blaring sounds]
- [Sachiko screaming]

13:02.948 --> 13:04.950
[music intensifying]

13:08.496 --> 13:09.789
[music fades]

13:09.872 --> 13:11.874
[humming]

13:13.083 --> 13:14.335
[wristband whirs]

13:15.961 --> 13:17.713
[chimes]

13:17.797 --> 13:19.340
- [whooshing]
- [noise stops]

13:19.423 --> 13:23.677
- [gasping]
- [computer] Room B3 has been unlocked.

13:23.761 --> 13:25.429
[suspenseful music playing]

13:26.096 --> 13:28.265
[gasps]

13:28.349 --> 13:29.934
Thank you!

13:30.518 --> 13:31.685
[sighs]

13:33.395 --> 13:37.608
A2 is a minus five points room.

13:38.526 --> 13:39.735
[beep]

13:39.819 --> 13:42.655
Points deduction confirmed.

13:53.707 --> 13:56.418
Twelfth round. Start.

14:02.883 --> 14:05.386
[Arisu] Okay, let's get
the wristband back.

14:06.470 --> 14:07.763
I'm coming.

14:08.264 --> 14:10.224
[Arisu] We'll open the door
from this side.

14:10.724 --> 14:13.853
Yuna will go in and take
the eight point deduction.

14:16.188 --> 14:17.189
Yuna, are you sure?

14:17.273 --> 14:20.234
Yes. When I'm inside, Usagi,

14:20.317 --> 14:23.028
retrieve your child's wristband
from inside the room.

14:24.280 --> 14:25.447
Thank you.

14:25.531 --> 14:27.032
We don't have much time.

14:27.116 --> 14:29.577
We need to do this
before the doors open and close.

14:30.077 --> 14:31.453
[Usagi] How long do we have?

14:31.954 --> 14:34.790
It's hard to tell precisely.
The timing can differ.

14:34.874 --> 14:39.044
The longest opening time is when
someone's standing in the doorway.

14:39.545 --> 14:41.922
[Usagi] Longest opening time? So how long?

14:42.006 --> 14:44.300
Ten seconds. Maximum.

14:46.176 --> 14:47.094
It's enough.

14:47.803 --> 14:51.015
[sighs] Let's do it. Is everyone ready?

14:52.266 --> 14:53.350
I'm ready.

14:55.936 --> 14:57.938
[dramatic music playing]

14:58.022 --> 14:59.398
[dice rattle]

15:12.411 --> 15:14.496
MOM, THANK YOU FOR EVERYTHING

15:17.666 --> 15:18.751
Ready?

15:19.418 --> 15:22.129
Ten seconds. I'll do the countdown.

15:29.345 --> 15:30.346
I'm going in.

15:35.976 --> 15:37.061
[gasps]

15:37.853 --> 15:38.979
What?

15:40.272 --> 15:41.440
- [Ryuji] Ten!
- [gasping]

15:44.276 --> 15:45.319
[Ryuji] Nine!

15:49.698 --> 15:50.616
Eight!

15:54.662 --> 15:56.705
- Seven!
- [Usagi panting]

15:58.749 --> 15:59.625
[Ryuji] Six!

16:03.712 --> 16:04.588
Five!

16:05.172 --> 16:06.006
[gasps]

16:06.090 --> 16:06.924
[Arisu] Hurry, Usagi!

16:09.760 --> 16:11.428
- [Ryuji] Four!
- [Usagi screams]

16:17.685 --> 16:18.602
Three!

16:25.901 --> 16:26.986
Two!

16:27.569 --> 16:30.280
This is a minus eight points room.

16:30.364 --> 16:33.325
- Usagi, run!
- Points deduction confirmed.

16:54.304 --> 16:55.889
[gasps]

17:02.980 --> 17:04.314
Arisu!

17:06.775 --> 17:07.609
Usagi!

17:08.610 --> 17:09.820
[Ryuji] One!

17:15.367 --> 17:16.493
Jump!

17:22.458 --> 17:24.460
[all panting]

17:42.436 --> 17:43.604
Thank you.

17:44.438 --> 17:45.856
[gasping shakily]

17:49.610 --> 17:51.612
[poignant music playing]

18:04.500 --> 18:06.085
[gasping]

18:06.168 --> 18:07.544
Arisu…

18:09.004 --> 18:10.881
what did your future hold?

18:30.692 --> 18:31.819
[PA chimes]

18:32.820 --> 18:38.117
All the players remaining in this room
shall be forced to stay.

18:38.909 --> 18:40.369
It's the last one, okay?

18:47.376 --> 18:48.919
[Ryuji grunting]

18:54.591 --> 18:55.634
Thank you.

19:01.723 --> 19:02.933
[sighs]

19:05.310 --> 19:08.188
Points deduction confirmed.

19:10.649 --> 19:12.776
[humming]

19:13.610 --> 19:16.905
Fourteenth round. Start.

19:17.906 --> 19:18.949
[die rattles]

19:19.449 --> 19:21.076
[chiming]

19:21.869 --> 19:23.787
[whirring]

19:28.208 --> 19:30.210
[tense, emotional music playing]

19:34.798 --> 19:36.800
[low rumbling]

19:42.639 --> 19:44.725
[baby crying]

19:44.808 --> 19:47.978
- [Yuna] Yu, are you okay? We're here!
- [woman] Please wait here.

19:48.520 --> 19:49.396
[Yuna] Yu!

19:50.981 --> 19:53.483
[man gasping shakily]

19:54.693 --> 19:56.069
[groans]

19:56.153 --> 19:59.114
[sobbing] You fool!

20:01.074 --> 20:02.659
[weeping]

20:06.997 --> 20:09.041
[grunting]

20:09.833 --> 20:11.668
[yells and groans]

20:12.544 --> 20:14.922
[woman] So what are you going
to do about this?

20:15.005 --> 20:16.673
[Nobu] I beg for your forgiveness.

20:16.757 --> 20:19.551
Bowing your head isn't going
to solve anything, young man.

20:19.635 --> 20:22.304
- This is a serious incident!
- [Nobu] I'm really… I'm sorry!

20:22.888 --> 20:23.972
Mother…

20:30.395 --> 20:32.272
[emotional music swells]

20:44.910 --> 20:45.994
EXIT

20:54.211 --> 20:55.504
Arisu…

20:56.588 --> 20:57.965
[Sachiko] What does that mean?

20:58.048 --> 21:00.467
I just saw an exit sign on the screen.

21:01.051 --> 21:02.844
It's the last room, isn't it?

21:03.345 --> 21:05.055
What's gonna happen now?

21:09.935 --> 21:10.769
[chiming]

21:10.852 --> 21:15.107
[computer] Players, hold your wristband
up to the chosen door

21:15.190 --> 21:17.734
and proceed to the next room.

21:20.362 --> 21:22.114
[sighs]

21:24.574 --> 21:25.492
Let's go.

21:25.575 --> 21:27.577
[intense, dramatic music playing]

21:40.382 --> 21:42.843
- Arisu…
- Nobu.

21:43.427 --> 21:44.845
[Usagi] Thank goodness.

21:50.267 --> 21:52.227
FIFTEENTH ROUND

21:52.311 --> 21:55.355
[Usagi] It's the last round.
We've just about made it.

21:55.439 --> 21:56.732
[music fades]

21:56.815 --> 22:00.485
[computer] You have all successfully
reached the exit room.

22:01.069 --> 22:02.154
[chimes]

22:02.237 --> 22:08.410
EXIT

22:12.956 --> 22:14.374
[whirring]

22:16.043 --> 22:17.252
[Usagi gasps]

22:19.338 --> 22:20.630
[sighs]

22:31.767 --> 22:32.976
[gasps softly]

22:35.020 --> 22:37.022
[silence]

22:47.866 --> 22:48.992
[PA chimes]

22:49.076 --> 22:52.245
Congratulations to everyone
who has reached the exit.

22:52.329 --> 22:55.207
It is time now to make
a final roll of the dice.

22:55.290 --> 22:56.833
[Nobu] A final roll?

22:56.917 --> 22:58.627
[chimes]

23:02.005 --> 23:03.840
[whirring]

23:07.135 --> 23:08.804
[Sachiko] We have to play again?

23:16.061 --> 23:17.646
[Arisu] I'll roll the dice.

23:18.939 --> 23:20.941
[tense music playing]

23:38.208 --> 23:39.918
I'll roll the dice

23:41.169 --> 23:42.629
and accept my fate.

23:43.463 --> 23:44.464
Arisu…

23:53.181 --> 23:54.683
[music fades]

24:03.775 --> 24:05.026
[emotional music playing]

24:07.529 --> 24:08.947
[chimes]

24:10.657 --> 24:12.701
[PA chimes]

24:12.784 --> 24:16.705
Seven players must now
proceed to the exit.

24:20.208 --> 24:21.751
[mechanism hisses]

24:22.794 --> 24:24.796
[wind gusting outside]

24:28.133 --> 24:29.301
Only seven.

24:29.885 --> 24:31.928
One of us has to stay.

24:36.433 --> 24:38.435
[breathes deeply]

24:49.863 --> 24:51.072
Usagi.

24:52.657 --> 24:53.909
You're in charge now.

24:54.784 --> 24:55.869
Huh?

24:56.912 --> 24:58.121
What are you saying?

24:58.205 --> 24:59.664
You have to live.

25:02.876 --> 25:04.794
Bring everyone back to our world.

25:05.295 --> 25:09.090
- [chiming]
- One minute remaining.

25:09.591 --> 25:11.301
- Usagi, please.
- Arisu!

25:11.384 --> 25:13.803
- This is what my future is.
- No!

25:13.887 --> 25:15.597
- You can't do this!
- Usagi.

25:15.680 --> 25:17.140
No! Don't leave me!

25:17.224 --> 25:18.475
- Usagi, please.
- No!

25:18.558 --> 25:21.311
- Usagi! Usagi…
- No, no, no, no! [sobbing]

25:21.394 --> 25:23.438
- No! [wailing]
- Listen up, everyone.

25:24.189 --> 25:27.150
- Take Usagi with you and live.
- [Usagi screams] No!

25:27.234 --> 25:28.318
Don't leave me!

25:28.401 --> 25:30.737
- Ryuji!
- Ryuji, please.

25:30.820 --> 25:32.531
Make sure she gets back to our world.

25:32.614 --> 25:34.241
- [Usagi] No!
- [Arisu] Please!

25:34.324 --> 25:36.993
- No! No!
- Thirty seconds remaining.

25:37.077 --> 25:39.287
- [Arisu] Hurry, all of you!
- You can't! Arisu!

25:39.371 --> 25:41.915
[Arisu] There's no more time!
Sachiko, hurry!

25:41.998 --> 25:43.917
[Usagi gasping] No, Arisu!

25:44.000 --> 25:45.794
- [Nobu] Hey…
- Arisu!

25:45.877 --> 25:49.381
[Arisu] Ryuji, make sure
Usagi gets back to our world.

25:49.464 --> 25:51.049
Ryuji, please!

25:51.550 --> 25:52.717
Promise me.

25:52.801 --> 25:55.554
[Usagi sobbing] Arisu! Arisu!

25:56.054 --> 25:57.389
[emotional music swells]

25:57.472 --> 25:58.723
No!

26:00.225 --> 26:01.977
No, wait, Arisu!

26:02.060 --> 26:04.563
[wailing] Arisu!

26:07.190 --> 26:09.484
No! Arisu!

26:10.694 --> 26:11.736
[music fades]

26:15.574 --> 26:16.908
[whirring]

26:17.909 --> 26:19.911
[dramatic music playing]

26:25.792 --> 26:27.043
[music fades]

26:30.714 --> 26:32.841
[whirring]

26:33.592 --> 26:35.302
[silence]

26:36.469 --> 26:37.846
[Usagi sobbing]

27:08.251 --> 27:10.253
[continues crying]

27:20.555 --> 27:24.351
Come with me… to the land of death.

27:26.895 --> 27:28.897
[suspenseful music playing]

27:31.399 --> 27:32.984
[Banda] If you kill Usagi,

27:33.068 --> 27:35.445
I promise to grant you your wish.

27:36.863 --> 27:39.658
I promise you will learn
about the land of the dead.

27:40.241 --> 27:42.786
A world beyond your wildest dreams.

27:47.040 --> 27:48.750
[Usagi continues sobbing]

28:04.474 --> 28:06.309
- What is he doing?
- [Usagi sobs]

28:11.606 --> 28:12.440
Usagi!

28:13.483 --> 28:16.194
Hey! Ryuji! What are you doing?

28:16.277 --> 28:19.614
Ryuji! Hey! Stop it, Ryuji! Stop!

28:19.698 --> 28:23.034
No! Stop it! Hey! Usagi! Hey!

28:23.618 --> 28:27.247
Ryuji! Don't do it! Stop!

28:28.790 --> 28:30.792
[music swells]

28:33.837 --> 28:36.047
Stop it! Hey!

28:36.131 --> 28:36.965
Stop it!

29:00.989 --> 29:02.991
[music quietens]

29:07.746 --> 29:09.330
[gasping]

29:15.170 --> 29:16.463
- [music fades]
- [PA chimes]

29:17.255 --> 29:19.257
Congratulations.

29:20.341 --> 29:23.595
You, the last remaining player
in this room,

29:23.678 --> 29:26.556
have entrusted everyone
with their futures.

29:26.639 --> 29:30.935
And for this reason,
you now also have a future.

29:31.686 --> 29:34.731
To the player who has
remained in this room,

29:34.814 --> 29:35.940
game cleared.

29:38.109 --> 29:39.444
What? [gasps]

29:40.195 --> 29:42.197
[dramatic music playing]

29:48.036 --> 29:49.537
[rumbling]

29:55.210 --> 29:57.212
[Usagi gasping]

30:00.965 --> 30:02.967
[intense crashing]

30:04.052 --> 30:05.762
[Sachiko shrieks]

30:05.845 --> 30:07.430
[metal groaning]

30:07.514 --> 30:08.723
[Sachiko yelps]

30:09.808 --> 30:11.851
[screaming]

30:39.879 --> 30:41.881
[all yelping]

30:46.135 --> 30:47.804
[all screaming]

30:51.057 --> 30:52.392
[gasps]

30:52.475 --> 30:53.685
[team gasping]

31:01.985 --> 31:03.319
Usagi!

31:04.487 --> 31:05.780
[Usagi shrieks]

31:05.864 --> 31:06.948
Usagi!

31:11.411 --> 31:13.413
[grunting]

31:27.927 --> 31:30.054
- [music fades]
- [whirring]

31:30.138 --> 31:31.764
[gasping]

31:32.724 --> 31:34.934
- [Banda] Congratulations, Arisu.
- [gasps]

31:39.397 --> 31:40.899
[humming]

31:48.907 --> 31:49.908
It's you.

31:50.408 --> 31:52.076
[ominous, dramatic music playing]

31:52.160 --> 31:55.079
Because you have succeeded
so brilliantly in winning,

31:55.163 --> 31:58.082
you now have the right
to become a citizen of this place.

31:58.833 --> 32:00.126
Become a citizen?

32:00.877 --> 32:02.629
I would never choose to stay here.

32:02.712 --> 32:05.924
You've been running after Usagi,
but she'll be dead soon.

32:06.424 --> 32:07.717
Come on, Arisu.

32:08.217 --> 32:11.429
Why not stay here,
and we can enjoy more games together?

32:13.556 --> 32:16.684
You brought me back to this place
just for your own entertainment?

32:17.268 --> 32:18.353
Of course.

32:19.145 --> 32:20.939
You had no right to do that.

32:22.398 --> 32:25.944
I knew you weren't the type of person
I could just summon here.

32:26.486 --> 32:29.113
So I decided to use Usagi as bait.

32:31.115 --> 32:33.910
You accepted to play the games
without hesitation.

32:35.411 --> 32:37.246
You bastard!

32:37.330 --> 32:38.957
- [clang]
- [grunts]

32:41.459 --> 32:42.794
[Arisu grunting]

32:42.877 --> 32:44.170
[Banda laughing]

32:44.754 --> 32:45.922
[yells]

32:46.005 --> 32:48.007
- [panting]
- [laughing]

32:52.053 --> 32:54.055
[laughing loudly]

32:58.309 --> 33:00.186
[continues laughing]

33:00.687 --> 33:02.647
[power crackles]

33:04.440 --> 33:06.192
[music fades]

33:06.275 --> 33:07.735
[panting]

33:27.296 --> 33:29.298
[dynamic music playing]

33:30.633 --> 33:31.718
[grunts]

33:32.969 --> 33:34.262
[hissing]

33:39.892 --> 33:40.852
[straining]

33:40.935 --> 33:42.437
[machinery grinding]

33:44.814 --> 33:46.149
[clanking]

33:47.066 --> 33:48.109
[grunts]

33:59.787 --> 34:01.581
[yells]

34:19.307 --> 34:21.350
- [Arisu] Are you okay?
- Arisu!

34:21.434 --> 34:23.352
- [Sachiko whimpers] I can't hold on!
- [Yuna] Help!

34:23.436 --> 34:24.520
[Usagi] Ryuji!

34:24.604 --> 34:25.897
[gasps]

34:25.980 --> 34:27.565
[Usagi] Ryuji!

34:29.067 --> 34:30.568
- Take my arm!
- [Nobu gasps]

34:33.821 --> 34:35.156
[Arisu] Sachiko!

34:36.324 --> 34:37.700
Give me your hand!

34:38.826 --> 34:40.536
[Sachiko gasping]

34:41.162 --> 34:42.622
Yuna, hold on!

34:44.040 --> 34:45.833
- [Arisu] You guys stay here!
- [Nobu] What?

34:48.711 --> 34:49.921
[Arisu] Usagi!

34:50.004 --> 34:51.172
[Usagi gasps]

34:56.844 --> 34:58.805
- [Nobu] Arisu!
- [Sachiko] Arisu!

34:59.263 --> 35:00.431
Arisu!

35:00.932 --> 35:03.768
- Quick! Go inside!
- Arisu!

35:04.894 --> 35:06.104
Usagi!

35:10.399 --> 35:11.692
Usagi!

35:13.820 --> 35:15.822
[Usagi gasps] Arisu!

35:19.242 --> 35:20.660
Usagi!

35:29.168 --> 35:30.461
[music fades]

35:34.257 --> 35:36.676
[echoing thud]

35:38.928 --> 35:40.930
[silence]

35:50.690 --> 35:52.692
[echoing rumble]

35:55.319 --> 35:57.446
[silence]

36:07.081 --> 36:09.083
[suspenseful music playing]

36:31.939 --> 36:33.816
[echoing thud]

36:35.443 --> 36:36.611
[Arisu] Usagi!

36:38.196 --> 36:39.405
[crash]

36:45.119 --> 36:47.121
[poignant music playing]

36:51.751 --> 36:53.377
It's all over now.

37:02.386 --> 37:04.013
[grunts]

37:19.445 --> 37:20.655
[Banda grunts]

37:35.503 --> 37:37.004
[music fades]

37:37.713 --> 37:38.881
Impossible.

37:40.675 --> 37:41.968
Can you see me?

37:42.051 --> 37:44.053
[dynamic music playing]

38:03.781 --> 38:05.116
Damn you!

38:17.878 --> 38:19.797
[screams]

38:19.880 --> 38:20.965
[gasps]

38:22.300 --> 38:23.384
Arisu?

38:24.427 --> 38:25.511
Arisu!

38:26.721 --> 38:29.015
Arisu! Arisu!

38:29.098 --> 38:31.058
You have to bring back Usagi!

38:31.642 --> 38:33.561
[Ann, echoing] Arisu!

38:33.644 --> 38:35.646
[music swells]

39:14.101 --> 39:16.687
[Banda] I expected
as much from you, Arisu.

39:16.771 --> 39:18.356
[music stops]

39:25.780 --> 39:28.282
Have you decided to stay here with me?

39:29.784 --> 39:31.786
[Arisu] No matter
how many times you ask me,

39:33.371 --> 39:35.414
I'll never accept to stay here.

39:39.418 --> 39:41.337
You've really disappointed me.

39:45.549 --> 39:47.843
Goodbye, Arisu. Game over.

40:01.816 --> 40:03.317
[man] I misjudged him.

40:03.401 --> 40:06.278
It appears he wasn't
quite ready for this role.

40:06.362 --> 40:08.114
[sounds fade]

40:08.197 --> 40:10.241
[footsteps echoing]

40:16.330 --> 40:18.332
[tense music playing]

40:29.427 --> 40:31.095
[rumbling, distorted laughter]

40:31.178 --> 40:32.054
[gasps]

40:36.725 --> 40:38.727
[creaking]

40:40.062 --> 40:43.107
[chants] Ohhh…

40:43.190 --> 40:45.192
[sounds return]

40:47.570 --> 40:49.238
[sounds fade]

40:59.665 --> 41:01.709
Are you the Joker?

41:03.544 --> 41:05.421
Who is the Joker?

41:06.088 --> 41:07.590
Who could it be?

41:07.673 --> 41:08.924
Is it God?

41:09.842 --> 41:11.051
Or is it me?

41:14.472 --> 41:16.390
Shall we play one last game?

41:19.727 --> 41:21.312
Please, have a seat.

41:25.441 --> 41:27.443
[shuffling cards]

41:29.737 --> 41:31.322
[Arisu gasping]

41:46.212 --> 41:48.797
Kindly choose one of these cards,
if you please.

41:49.590 --> 41:52.176
Your choice of card will
determine your fate.

41:55.221 --> 42:00.643
However, if you choose the Joker,
then I shall win the game.

42:00.726 --> 42:04.813
And so your destiny shall
be decided by me alone.

42:55.155 --> 42:59.034
So it is.
And now your destiny belongs to me.

43:00.578 --> 43:02.997
Both cards are Jokers, isn't that right?

43:08.919 --> 43:10.588
What a coincidence.

43:12.131 --> 43:13.882
[Arisu] Cut the bullshit.

43:13.966 --> 43:15.634
You're cheating, period.

43:16.468 --> 43:17.845
[man] Listen, young man.

43:18.637 --> 43:22.641
Every deck of cards contains
four suits of 13 cards each.

43:23.642 --> 43:27.062
Add up the value of each card,
you get 364.

43:27.605 --> 43:31.400
When you then add the Joker, you get 365.

43:31.483 --> 43:36.238
Exactly the number of days
as in a year in your world.

43:36.739 --> 43:38.407
[eerie music playing]

43:38.490 --> 43:41.994
And if you add another Joker, you get 366.

43:42.077 --> 43:44.371
The same number of days as in a leap year.

43:46.832 --> 43:48.250
So you see,

43:48.834 --> 43:53.297
the two Joker cards are necessary based
on the truth of human time constructs.

43:55.299 --> 43:56.550
The Joker is a jester

43:56.634 --> 44:01.013
who fills in the gaps between the cards,
between the gaps in time.

44:01.096 --> 44:05.601
And he fills in the gaps
between life and death.

44:07.728 --> 44:09.480
So are you the Joker?

44:10.064 --> 44:11.523
You misunderstand.

44:12.024 --> 44:13.901
The Joker is not a person.

44:14.693 --> 44:17.696
Neither is it an entity
that controls this world.

44:17.780 --> 44:20.949
Nor an entity that oversees
the games we play.

44:21.492 --> 44:22.618
The Joker

44:23.452 --> 44:24.703
is just a card.

44:29.958 --> 44:32.544
You are a very interesting human.

44:34.004 --> 44:36.674
And I believe
that it is not entirely a coincidence

44:36.757 --> 44:40.886
that both the cards that determined
your destiny were Jokers.

44:41.929 --> 44:45.015
Your fate is in my hands.

44:45.099 --> 44:47.810
It is mine to do as I please.

44:50.396 --> 44:51.230
But…

44:52.773 --> 44:55.484
in consideration of this coincidence,

44:55.567 --> 44:58.278
I have decided to offer you a choice.

44:58.362 --> 45:00.364
[muffled rumbling]

45:06.578 --> 45:08.580
[man] You will find death

45:09.456 --> 45:11.125
just over there.

45:32.062 --> 45:34.064
[quiet, emotional music playing]

45:42.281 --> 45:46.577
[man] That vortex will drag you down,
and you will die.

45:55.836 --> 45:58.130
Over there, you will find life.

46:01.091 --> 46:05.304
Life is painful,
filled with many trials to endure.

46:05.804 --> 46:07.389
Death, on the other hand,

46:07.473 --> 46:11.435
is accepting the way of the universe
until you reach its natural end.

46:13.437 --> 46:15.272
Which path do you chose?

46:17.399 --> 46:19.693
Everyone passes through this place.

46:20.277 --> 46:24.698
This is… the world between life and death.

46:25.491 --> 46:28.035
Even if you return
to the world of the living,

46:28.577 --> 46:30.162
your time will come,

46:31.079 --> 46:33.332
and eventually, you'll be back here.

46:34.249 --> 46:35.626
In the end,

46:37.002 --> 46:39.129
everyone takes the path of the dead.

46:40.339 --> 46:44.343
All the same,
do you wish to return to your world,

46:44.426 --> 46:46.678
even if it means suffering and pain?

46:50.724 --> 46:53.227
If you choose to return to your world,

46:54.019 --> 46:56.855
the woman you are searching for,
and the baby,

46:56.939 --> 46:58.690
may no longer be there.

47:00.025 --> 47:02.694
The path of death is the easier way.

47:04.321 --> 47:06.824
Just throw yourself into the vortex.

47:07.491 --> 47:11.787
It's quite… empty,
emptier than you can imagine.

47:13.330 --> 47:14.790
There's no more pain.

47:15.415 --> 47:16.667
No more suffering.

47:17.709 --> 47:19.545
And no happiness, either.

47:22.089 --> 47:23.799
[chuckling]

47:27.886 --> 47:29.847
What is your purpose in this place?

47:32.516 --> 47:34.268
I am the watchman.

47:35.060 --> 47:36.979
My purpose, you see,

47:37.062 --> 47:40.274
is solely to watch the space
between life and death.

47:41.942 --> 47:43.318
Everybody dies.

47:45.821 --> 47:48.532
I serve as the watchman
at the gates of death,

47:49.825 --> 47:52.786
and for my services, death passes me by.

47:55.038 --> 47:57.499
You recommend death to everyone,

47:58.333 --> 48:00.586
and yet you're afraid of death yourself.

48:03.463 --> 48:05.048
You might be right.

48:07.467 --> 48:09.595
[Arisu] Is that why you gave me a choice?

48:10.554 --> 48:15.851
I was interested in the opinion of someone
who has survived death many times.

48:21.899 --> 48:24.902
Soon this place shall be flooded
with many people.

48:26.278 --> 48:27.529
Flooded?

48:32.159 --> 48:33.368
What will happen?

48:35.579 --> 48:36.872
Something

48:37.956 --> 48:40.125
much, much bigger than before.

48:40.834 --> 48:43.128
Much bigger than that
which brought you here.

48:45.380 --> 48:47.382
How many people are going to die?

48:48.884 --> 48:50.844
That is none of my concern.

48:53.138 --> 48:58.143
[chants loudly] Ohhh…

48:58.226 --> 49:00.228
[sounds return]

49:09.154 --> 49:12.574
It is time for you to choose your path.

49:18.038 --> 49:20.832
I will return to the world
of the living with Usagi.

49:20.916 --> 49:22.918
[dramatic music playing]

49:24.127 --> 49:25.545
[Usagi screams] No!

49:26.463 --> 49:27.547
Usagi?

49:28.548 --> 49:31.134
[Usagi gasping]

49:33.887 --> 49:35.806
[screaming]

49:35.889 --> 49:37.474
Usagi!

49:37.557 --> 49:38.809
Choose…

49:40.936 --> 49:42.187
your destiny.

49:53.991 --> 49:57.202
You are indeed
a truly interesting specimen.

49:58.537 --> 50:00.539
[dramatic music swells]

50:05.502 --> 50:07.629
[deep rumbling]

50:19.057 --> 50:20.267
Usagi!

50:25.355 --> 50:26.565
[deep groaning]

50:26.648 --> 50:28.608
[heavy creaking]

50:33.947 --> 50:35.198
Arisu!

50:35.782 --> 50:37.159
Usagi!

50:38.535 --> 50:40.412
[intense crashing]

50:42.998 --> 50:45.375
- [Ryuji] Let's go together.
- [Usagi shrieks]

50:45.459 --> 50:46.460
Arisu!

50:47.836 --> 50:49.671
Hey! Ryuji!

51:03.977 --> 51:06.271
[Ryuji] Let's go
to the land of death together.

51:06.354 --> 51:07.272
[Usagi gasps] What?

51:08.440 --> 51:09.441
No! Stop!

51:09.524 --> 51:11.193
Ryuji! [gasping]

51:12.194 --> 51:13.737
[Arisu] Usagi!

51:13.820 --> 51:15.197
- Ryuji!
- [Usagi screams]

51:15.280 --> 51:16.490
[Arisu] Don't die!

51:18.241 --> 51:19.493
[Usagi] No!

51:21.453 --> 51:24.081
[Arisu] Stop! Ryuji!

51:31.463 --> 51:33.757
[gasping]

51:34.758 --> 51:35.967
[inaudible]

51:47.854 --> 51:49.106
[panting]

51:50.607 --> 51:51.817
[Usagi] Arisu!

51:52.901 --> 51:54.694
[gasps] Arisu!

51:58.281 --> 52:00.033
[Arisu] Usagi!

52:00.117 --> 52:02.119
- Usagi!
- [Usagi gasps]

52:02.202 --> 52:03.203
No!

52:03.870 --> 52:04.913
[sobbing]

52:04.996 --> 52:06.164
Usagi!

52:07.999 --> 52:10.293
[sobbing] Arisu!

52:10.377 --> 52:11.837
Arisu! [gasps]

52:11.920 --> 52:13.755
[Arisu] Usagi!

52:14.256 --> 52:16.258
[spluttering]

52:16.341 --> 52:17.467
[sounds fade]

52:18.051 --> 52:19.553
[Usagi sobs]

52:20.971 --> 52:22.931
[emotional music playing]

52:30.981 --> 52:32.149
[spluttering]

52:34.734 --> 52:36.403
Arisu!

52:37.028 --> 52:38.530
Arisu!

52:39.406 --> 52:41.867
Arisu! Arisu!

52:43.201 --> 52:44.244
[Arisu] Promise me.

52:44.327 --> 52:46.413
Make sure Usagi gets back to our world!

52:46.496 --> 52:48.081
- Ryuji, please!
- [Usagi sobbing]

52:48.165 --> 52:49.291
[Ryuji sighs]

52:50.917 --> 52:52.711
[emotional music swells]

52:58.300 --> 53:00.218
[Ryuji groaning]

53:00.302 --> 53:02.012
[Usagi sobbing]

53:03.388 --> 53:04.389
[yells]

53:08.351 --> 53:09.728
[groaning]

53:14.816 --> 53:16.067
[screams]

53:21.323 --> 53:22.616
[groans]

53:22.699 --> 53:23.950
[yells]

53:25.118 --> 53:26.536
- [gasps]
- [Usagi sobs]

53:32.918 --> 53:34.252
Keep on living.

53:34.753 --> 53:36.588
[gasping]

53:41.092 --> 53:42.469
Ryuji!

53:53.605 --> 53:55.398
[crashing]

54:11.539 --> 54:13.541
[emotional music swells]

54:58.920 --> 55:00.297
[music fades]

55:00.380 --> 55:01.715
[father] Usagi…

55:05.885 --> 55:07.887
[breathing shakily]

55:10.015 --> 55:12.017
[wind whistling softly]

55:19.399 --> 55:20.567
My daughter.

55:22.610 --> 55:23.945
Father?

55:25.071 --> 55:26.239
[Usagi gasps]

55:28.616 --> 55:29.784
[gasps]

55:36.833 --> 55:38.752
[gasps]

55:40.462 --> 55:41.921
[sighs]

55:42.714 --> 55:44.507
[quiet, emotional music playing]

55:47.761 --> 55:49.179
[tearfully] Father…

55:52.349 --> 55:54.267
I've missed you so much.

55:56.686 --> 55:58.146
[sobbing]

55:59.064 --> 56:00.732
In the world of the living,

56:01.566 --> 56:03.360
I was so happy with you.

56:07.781 --> 56:09.074
Dad…

56:12.577 --> 56:14.204
[breathing shakily]

56:19.793 --> 56:21.961
I want you to live, Usagi.

56:23.088 --> 56:24.964
I want you to be happy too.

56:26.299 --> 56:27.467
[gasps]

56:29.177 --> 56:30.220
[sobs]

56:42.774 --> 56:44.234
[gasps]

57:01.084 --> 57:02.836
[emotional music continues]

57:07.090 --> 57:08.174
Arisu!

57:12.512 --> 57:14.139
[music swells]

58:58.076 --> 58:59.410
[music fades]

59:06.417 --> 59:07.710
[gasps]

59:09.337 --> 59:10.755
Arisu…

59:33.194 --> 59:36.030
How long have I been gone?

59:38.575 --> 59:39.784
Two minutes.

59:41.286 --> 59:42.787
You just made it out.

59:45.206 --> 59:47.709
A few seconds more
and you might not have made it.

59:48.918 --> 59:52.505
[gasps] And Usagi? What happened to her?

59:55.008 --> 59:57.802
Well, you should know that
better than anyone, Arisu.

59:59.846 --> 01:00:00.680
I gotta go.

01:00:00.763 --> 01:00:02.098
- [Ann] Oh!
- [groans]

01:00:02.181 --> 01:00:03.891
[winces] I'm okay.

01:00:12.108 --> 01:00:15.361
Thank you… Ann.

01:00:17.238 --> 01:00:18.656
[gentle music playing]

01:00:22.994 --> 01:00:24.203
[door closes]

01:00:43.931 --> 01:00:45.933
[monitor beeping regularly]

01:00:46.017 --> 01:00:47.226
Usagi.

01:01:10.833 --> 01:01:12.251
You're okay.

01:01:15.004 --> 01:01:17.090
[stomach rumbles]

01:01:19.801 --> 01:01:20.968
[Arisu gasps]

01:01:21.511 --> 01:01:23.638
I'm hungry…

01:01:30.061 --> 01:01:31.270
[sighs]

01:01:34.482 --> 01:01:35.942
Arisu!

01:01:37.026 --> 01:01:38.111
[laughs]

01:02:10.935 --> 01:02:12.937
[poignant music playing]

01:02:16.149 --> 01:02:17.608
[birdsong]

01:02:22.280 --> 01:02:24.449
Well, because the baby will
be born during the summer…

01:02:24.532 --> 01:02:26.117
We can use the kanji sign for summer…

01:02:26.200 --> 01:02:28.411
- Natsumi.
- Natsumi.

01:02:28.911 --> 01:02:30.621
- [Arisu] And the kanji for beauty.
- Mm.

01:02:30.705 --> 01:02:32.582
- [Arisu] Natsuki.
- [Usagi] Natsuki…

01:02:32.665 --> 01:02:34.167
RINKA, NATSUKI, KANADE,
KOHARU, NATSUMI

01:02:34.250 --> 01:02:35.334
[sighs]

01:02:36.544 --> 01:02:38.838
- Let me think. What else?
- Mm…

01:02:39.422 --> 01:02:40.590
Look! Generosity.

01:02:40.673 --> 01:02:42.633
- Huh. Hiro?
- Uh-huh.

01:02:43.342 --> 01:02:44.886
It's difficult.

01:02:44.969 --> 01:02:47.597
We already picked a lot of good names.

01:02:47.680 --> 01:02:50.141
But now we really need to narrow it down.

01:02:50.224 --> 01:02:52.393
If we just keep making
a list of good names,

01:02:52.477 --> 01:02:54.812
we'll never make our minds up.

01:02:54.896 --> 01:02:57.648
Hmm. One more…

01:03:00.568 --> 01:03:03.112
Usagi, let's pick the one you prefer.

01:03:03.196 --> 01:03:04.864
[sighs] Typical.

01:03:04.947 --> 01:03:06.991
The usual answer from men who don't care.

01:03:07.074 --> 01:03:08.409
No, no!

01:03:08.493 --> 01:03:10.661
I do care and I am thinking about it,

01:03:10.745 --> 01:03:12.872
but it seems to me that

01:03:13.372 --> 01:03:15.333
your name can decide your fate.

01:03:15.416 --> 01:03:17.585
Why me? [sighs]

01:03:18.669 --> 01:03:20.171
It's better that you decide.

01:03:20.254 --> 01:03:22.423
No way! We decide together!

01:03:25.134 --> 01:03:27.094
- Ah, I'm late!
- Hm?

01:03:27.178 --> 01:03:28.346
I have to go.

01:03:29.472 --> 01:03:32.058
You think you can just leave like that?

01:03:35.436 --> 01:03:37.063
I will never leave you.

01:03:37.563 --> 01:03:38.898
I promise, my love.

01:03:41.150 --> 01:03:42.568
I love you too.

01:03:44.487 --> 01:03:47.657
So then when you come back,
we find that name.

01:03:47.740 --> 01:03:50.535
- Huh?
- Tonight we name our child!

01:03:50.618 --> 01:03:51.994
Run! Until tonight!

01:03:53.079 --> 01:03:54.413
I'll see you later.

01:03:59.627 --> 01:04:01.462
[poignant music continues]

01:04:12.890 --> 01:04:14.851
I wanna say thanks, Mom.

01:04:14.934 --> 01:04:17.395
It's all thanks to you
that I could graduate.

01:04:17.478 --> 01:04:19.313
You know that's not true.

01:04:20.815 --> 01:04:22.650
Well, it's my turn now.

01:04:22.733 --> 01:04:23.901
Your turn?

01:04:24.402 --> 01:04:27.822
To make you happy, Mom.
It's my turn to take care of you now.

01:04:28.489 --> 01:04:29.824
[both laugh]

01:04:30.825 --> 01:04:32.493
I think I'm better at that game.

01:04:32.577 --> 01:04:33.995
[both laugh]

01:04:34.745 --> 01:04:36.122
- [Yuna] I had an idea.
- [Ken] Yeah?

01:04:36.205 --> 01:04:38.374
- I'd like us to visit his grave together.
- [Ken] Really?

01:04:38.457 --> 01:04:42.128
[Yuna] Yeah. I think it's about time
I introduced you to my brother.

01:04:42.211 --> 01:04:44.088
"Sohta, this is my boyfriend."

01:04:44.171 --> 01:04:45.756
- [Ken] You're right.
- [Yuna] Yeah.

01:04:45.840 --> 01:04:48.551
- Well, then I have a lot to think about.
- [Yuna] Like what?

01:04:48.634 --> 01:04:51.178
- Well, like, what to say, what to wear…
- None of that's important.

01:04:51.262 --> 01:04:52.597
You have to do these things right!

01:04:52.680 --> 01:04:55.391
- Okay, so what'll you wear?
- Hmm, let me think…

01:04:55.474 --> 01:04:56.642
Maybe I should wear a suit.

01:04:56.726 --> 01:04:59.645
[Sachiko] You're no longer a child.
You have to take care of yourself.

01:04:59.729 --> 01:05:01.397
You'll soon be in high school.

01:05:01.480 --> 01:05:02.940
[son] Yeah, I know.

01:05:03.024 --> 01:05:05.401
Sometimes I wonder who you take after.

01:05:05.484 --> 01:05:07.737
After you, Mom, that's obvious.

01:05:08.404 --> 01:05:09.405
Really?

01:05:10.156 --> 01:05:11.282
[laughs]

01:05:11.365 --> 01:05:12.408
Obviously!

01:05:12.491 --> 01:05:13.743
[both laugh]

01:05:13.826 --> 01:05:15.369
[Rei] I read your letter.

01:05:16.245 --> 01:05:18.706
Thanks, Mom, for watching the show.

01:05:19.498 --> 01:05:23.002
Mmm. I got a job working
on a new anime project.

01:05:23.669 --> 01:05:27.173
Mmm. And this time, it's gonna be a movie.

01:05:27.256 --> 01:05:30.134
[laughs] You and Dad can
go watch it together.

01:05:30.635 --> 01:05:32.094
'Kay. [chuckles]

01:05:33.220 --> 01:05:35.014
ARISU

01:05:37.850 --> 01:05:39.644
[woman] Thank you for your visit.

01:05:39.727 --> 01:05:42.063
Would you like
to make your next appointment?

01:05:42.563 --> 01:05:45.608
[man] Do you have any availabilities
around mid-May?

01:05:45.691 --> 01:05:47.526
Let me check the appointments.

01:05:47.610 --> 01:05:48.903
[music fades]

01:05:48.986 --> 01:05:53.032
What do you do
that gives your life a sense of meaning?

01:05:53.115 --> 01:05:54.659
[woman] A sense of meaning?

01:05:56.410 --> 01:05:57.620
[sighs]

01:05:57.703 --> 01:05:59.205
[quiet, contemplative music playing]

01:06:00.456 --> 01:06:03.292
Well, I guess when I'm in the dojo,
practicing karate.

01:06:03.793 --> 01:06:05.503
I thought you had stopped karate?

01:06:05.586 --> 01:06:09.048
[chuckles] Well, actually,
I started teaching at my father's club.

01:06:09.924 --> 01:06:12.510
When I see all those kids
practicing so hard,

01:06:13.135 --> 01:06:14.762
that's what gives me meaning.

01:06:14.845 --> 01:06:16.555
It makes me happy.

01:06:17.682 --> 01:06:18.766
[chuckles]

01:06:20.059 --> 01:06:21.018
[laughs]

01:06:22.770 --> 01:06:25.189
Are you still having some flashbacks?

01:06:26.357 --> 01:06:29.068
Lately, I've been sleeping a lot better.

01:06:29.568 --> 01:06:30.945
And my job's going well.

01:06:31.612 --> 01:06:32.989
Well, that's good to hear.

01:06:33.781 --> 01:06:35.324
You told me that since the event,

01:06:35.408 --> 01:06:38.369
you've been thinking a lot
about the meaning of life.

01:06:40.579 --> 01:06:44.166
I ask myself,
"What's the point in living?"

01:06:49.463 --> 01:06:50.923
Maybe for this hat?

01:06:51.507 --> 01:06:53.759
Stopping the shop from going bust?

01:07:00.725 --> 01:07:02.560
[sighs]

01:07:03.144 --> 01:07:06.272
[Arisu] What are the things
that give meaning to your life now?

01:07:06.355 --> 01:07:10.735
It's important to me that people see me
as a role model and as an influencer.

01:07:13.529 --> 01:07:17.074
That way…
That way I can get to see the world.

01:07:22.872 --> 01:07:24.498
You're very courageous.

01:07:25.374 --> 01:07:26.709
[chuckles]

01:07:28.335 --> 01:07:32.423
[Arisu] What is it that gives you a sense
of purpose, a sense of meaning in life?

01:07:33.632 --> 01:07:35.801
For a long time, I really didn't know.

01:07:36.302 --> 01:07:38.888
I didn't understand why I was still alive.

01:07:40.139 --> 01:07:42.016
But lately, I've realized that

01:07:42.099 --> 01:07:44.894
coming to terms with my being alive
is my mission in life.

01:07:47.980 --> 01:07:49.231
So, right now…

01:07:49.857 --> 01:07:52.610
[sighs] …I work with kids
that are in trouble.

01:07:54.070 --> 01:07:55.112
[chuckles]

01:07:57.782 --> 01:07:58.824
[man] Meaning?

01:08:01.035 --> 01:08:02.161
Hmm.

01:08:04.371 --> 01:08:06.749
That's a good question. [sighs]

01:08:07.917 --> 01:08:09.919
[emotional music swells]

01:08:18.469 --> 01:08:20.346
Even if I don't know,

01:08:21.222 --> 01:08:22.723
it's not that important.

01:08:23.349 --> 01:08:24.975
Life can still be good.

01:08:26.560 --> 01:08:27.812
That's very true.

01:08:30.731 --> 01:08:32.108
And what about you?

01:08:33.109 --> 01:08:35.653
What is it that gives
meaning to your life?

01:08:36.570 --> 01:08:37.988
What keeps you alive?

01:08:38.572 --> 01:08:39.490
Huh?

01:08:41.450 --> 01:08:43.202
That's a really good question.

01:08:44.411 --> 01:08:46.997
Hmm, today, I'd say…

01:08:48.415 --> 01:08:51.168
it's about picking names for my child.

01:08:53.921 --> 01:08:54.922
Wow.

01:08:57.341 --> 01:08:58.592
[chuckles]

01:09:04.473 --> 01:09:05.724
[music fades]

01:09:10.855 --> 01:09:13.149
- [woman 1] I'll leave this here.
- [woman 2] Thank you.

01:09:13.232 --> 01:09:15.234
[rattling]

01:09:20.739 --> 01:09:23.701
[low rumbling]

01:09:23.784 --> 01:09:26.078
- Another one.
- [woman 1] Is it another earthquake?

01:09:26.162 --> 01:09:27.246
[man] Mm-hmm.

01:09:37.339 --> 01:09:38.549
[rattling subsides]

01:09:39.216 --> 01:09:42.052
- I think it's over, right?
- Mmm.

01:09:43.053 --> 01:09:45.389
- There was a big one earlier too.
- Mmm.

01:09:45.472 --> 01:09:48.267
- We seem to be having a lot.
- Yeah, you're right.

01:09:48.350 --> 01:09:49.935
[woman 2] I wonder if it's on the news?

01:09:51.061 --> 01:09:54.106
Reports are coming in of an earthquake
off the coast of Chiba,

01:09:54.190 --> 01:09:57.484
approximately 40 miles below
the earth's surface.

01:09:57.568 --> 01:10:00.863
The government advised
that there is zero risk of tsunami.

01:10:01.363 --> 01:10:04.366
News is coming in about another
earthquake in the Kantō region,

01:10:04.450 --> 01:10:06.577
measuring five on the Richter scale.

01:10:06.660 --> 01:10:10.247
It appears now that seismic activity
has been recorded simultaneously

01:10:10.331 --> 01:10:14.335
in multiple locations around the planet,
including California in the United States.

01:10:14.418 --> 01:10:17.755
Experts are suggesting this may be a sign
of tectonic movement on a global scale…

01:10:17.838 --> 01:10:20.633
[man 2] …regions in Japan,
parts of Europe and the US West Coast.

01:10:20.716 --> 01:10:24.178
Experts are now suggesting
that global environmental changes

01:10:24.261 --> 01:10:26.847
may be having an impact
on seismic activity

01:10:26.931 --> 01:10:29.850
which could potentially trigger
these simultaneous tremors.

01:10:29.934 --> 01:10:33.145
Seismologists are calling
the unprecedented series of earthquakes

01:10:33.229 --> 01:10:35.481
an extremely rare phenomenon,

01:10:35.564 --> 01:10:38.651
indicating a major concern
for the trigger effect…

01:10:38.734 --> 01:10:40.861
[server] Hey, guys, are you ready?

01:10:41.779 --> 01:10:43.781
[woman] Yeah, okay, okay, okay.

01:10:46.533 --> 01:10:47.952
[man 1] Everybody, right?

01:10:48.035 --> 01:10:49.662
How you doin'? Can we get a table for two?

01:10:49.745 --> 01:10:51.747
And, uh, by the window if you can.

01:10:51.830 --> 01:10:52.873
Thank you.

01:10:53.791 --> 01:10:55.125
Been watching the playoffs, right?

01:10:55.209 --> 01:10:56.669
- Nah, I haven't.
- What?

01:10:56.752 --> 01:10:58.295
- Yeah, man.
- Not one game?

01:10:58.379 --> 01:10:59.421
Has it been good?

01:10:59.505 --> 01:11:02.841
Bro, best series
I've probably seen since 2010.

01:11:02.925 --> 01:11:03.968
- No way.
- Easily.

01:11:04.051 --> 01:11:05.427
- No, I don't believe you.
- Easily.

01:11:05.511 --> 01:11:07.763
- I might have to check it out.
- You gotta check it out.

01:11:07.846 --> 01:11:09.515
Can I have a beer on tap, please?

01:11:09.598 --> 01:11:11.850
I'll do the same.
And then a couple waters as well.

01:11:12.351 --> 01:11:14.812
- Best series since 2010?
- Yeah, bro, you gotta…

01:11:16.522 --> 01:11:18.524
[dramatic music playing]
